/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.1 Concept and Industrial Applications of Surface Development) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(The development of a surface is the complete unfolding or unrolling of all outer) Tj
T*
(bounding surfaces of a 3D solid onto a flat 2D plane without stretching, tearing, or) Tj
T*
(distortion:) Tj
T*
(* Industrial Relevance: Essential for sheet metal fabrication, duct design \(HVAC\),) Tj
T*
(pipe bends, chemical hoppers, aircraft fairings, boiler shells, and packaging design.) Tj
T*
(* True Length Principle: Every line and boundary edge drawn in a surface development) Tj
T*
(must show its TRUE LENGTH \(TL\). Apparent foreshortened lengths from orthographic) Tj
T*
(views cannot be used directly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.2 Classification of Surface Development Methods) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* 1. Parallel-Line Development: Used for solids having uniform parallel edges or) Tj
T*
(generators \(Prisms and Cylinders\). The stretch-out line is a straight line) Tj
T*
(perpendicular to the axis, with length equal to the perimeter of the base.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Radial-Line Development: Used for solids with converging edges or generators) Tj
T*
(meeting at a single apex \(Pyramids and Cones\). The development is formed by radiating) Tj
T*
(circular arcs centered at the apex, with radius equal to True Slant Height.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Triangulation Development: Used for transition pieces, hoppers, and irregular) Tj
T*
(non-developable shapes. The surface is divided into a mesh of contiguous triangles) Tj
T*
(whose true edge lengths are found and laid out consecutively.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Approximate Development: Used for double-curved surfaces that are mathematically) Tj
T*
(non-developable \(Spheres, paraboloids\) by dividing into spherical zones \(lunettes\) or) Tj
T*
(gore strips.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.3 Development of Truncated Solids and Cones) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Truncated Prism: Stretch-out line length = Perimeter \(n x side\). Vertical fold) Tj
T*
(lines spaced by side width. Heights of cut points measured directly from elevation) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
