(>> 6.4 AutoCAD 3D Boolean Operations and Visual Styles) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Boolean Solid Modeling Commands:) Tj
T*
(- UNION \(UNI\): Merges two or more overlapping 3D solids or 2D regions into a single) Tj
T*
(seamless continuous solid entity.) Tj
T*
(- SUBTRACT \(SU\): Removes the volume of selected tool solids from the designated base) Tj
T*
(solid \(Base Solid - Tool Solid\).) Tj
T*
(- INTERSECT \(IN\): Calculates and retains only the common overlapping intersecting volume) Tj
T*
(shared between two or more solids.) Tj
T*
(* 3D Navigation & Inspection:) Tj
T*
(- 3DORBIT \(3DO\): Dynamically rotates 3D model view in real time about target point.) Tj
T*
(- NAVISWHEEL: Unified steering wheel providing Pan, Zoom, Orbit, Rewind, and Look) Tj
T*
(functions.) Tj
T*
(* Visual Styles \(VS\):) Tj
T*
(- 2D Wireframe: Basic vector lines and arcs representing edges.) Tj
T*
(- Conceptual: Smooth shaded surface with cool-to-warm color transitions based on face) Tj
T*
(normals.) Tj
T*
(- Hidden: Displays solid geometry while suppressing hidden back lines.) Tj
T*
(- Realistic: Displays solid models with realistic materials, textures, and lighting.) Tj
T*
(- Shaded with Edges: Optimal engineering drafting mode displaying crisp black boundary) Tj
T*
(edges over shaded faces.) Tj
T*
(* Mass Properties \(MASSPROP\): Calculates volume, mass, bounding box, center of) Tj
T*
(gravity \(centroid\), moments of inertia, and radii of gyration for any 3D solid.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
