(development of the lateral surface of the truncated prism.) Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Construction Procedure:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Front View & Section Plane:) Tj
T*
(- Draw Front View of hexagonal prism: Base line = 60 mm, Height = 70 mm.) Tj
T*
(- Axis passes at x = 30 mm. Mark cut center at height 40 mm on axis.) Tj
T*
(- Draw cutting plane at 45 degrees inclined to base passing through \(30, 40\).) Tj
T*
(- Label intersection points with vertical edges: 1'', 2'', 3'', 4'', 5'', 6''.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Stretch-Out Line Formulation:) Tj
T*
(- Stretch-out line length = 6 x side = 6 x 30 mm = 180 mm.) Tj
T*
(- Divide into 6 equal segments of 30 mm labeled A, B, C, D, E, F, A \(seam at A\).) Tj
T*
(- Erect vertical lines of height 70 mm at each division representing vertical edges.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Transferring True Cut Heights:) Tj
T*
(- Since vertical edges of the prism are perpendicular to HP, their elevation views show) Tj
T*
(TRUE LENGTHS directly!) Tj
T*
(- Project cut point 1'' horizontally to edges A; point 2'' to edge B; point 3'' to edge) Tj
T*
(C; point 4'' to edge D; point 5'' to edge E; point 6'' to edge F.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Boundary Profiling: Connect points 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 1 with straight lines) Tj
T*
(\(since prism faces are flat planar facets\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([PROBLEM 2: Radial-Line Development of a Truncated Right Circular Cone]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: A right circular cone of base diameter 60 mm and altitude 80 mm rests) Tj
T*
(on its base on HP. It is cut by a section plane inclined at 30 degrees to HP, bisecting) Tj
T*
(the cone axis. Draw the development of the remaining truncated cone surface.) Tj
T*
(Mathematical Derivation & Geometric Protocol:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Calculate True Slant Height \(L\):) Tj
T*
(- Radius R = 60 / 2 = 30 mm. Height H = 80 mm.) Tj
T*
(- Slant Height L = sqrt\(R^2 + H^2\) = sqrt\(30^2 + 80^2\) = sqrt\(900 + 6400\) = sqrt\(7300\) =) Tj
T*
(85.44 mm.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Calculate Sector Development Angle \(theta\):) Tj
T*
(- theta = \(R / L\) x 360 deg = \(30 / 85.44\) x 360 deg = 0.3511 x 360 = 126.4 degrees.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Radial Sector Layout:) Tj
T*
(- Center at Apex O, strike a circular arc of radius L = 85.44 mm.) Tj
T*
(- Measure sector angle theta = 126.4 degrees using protractor. Divide sector into 12) Tj
T*
(equal angles \(10.53 deg each\) representing 12 cone generators.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Finding True Cut Generator Lengths:) Tj
T*
(- Section plane bisects axis at height H/2 = 40 mm. Draw 30-deg cut plane.) Tj
T*
(- Only the extreme contour generators O-1'' and O-7'' in elevation show True Length.) Tj
T*
(- For intermediate generators \(2, 3, 4, 5, 6\), project intersection points HORIZONTALLY) Tj
T*
(onto the extreme contour generator O-7'' to measure their true distances from apex O.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
